Subject: [PATCH v10 5/6] jails/instances/lab-mail: Serve the mirror over IMAP
 with Dovecot
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: ppsyqmxwvnrsywsmxltxwsntzvtmzsqq

Agents need to read list mail without the Fastmail credentials, and
from any host that might run them later. Dovecot serves the local
maildir over IMAP on loopback, so a client needs a network address
and not a shared filesystem, and keeps working while Fastmail is
down.

The mailbox is read-only twice over. An ACL grants clients only list
and read, and Dovecot runs as a user that cannot write the maildir.
Clients log in with any name and password, since IMAP has no
anonymous mode and loopback is the boundary.
